  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WeBelong Phase II: Regional Migration and Development Program contributing toward the Sida 2021-2025 Regional LAC Strategy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The social, economic and political context in the Latin America and the Caribbean (LAC) region remains challenging, affecting migration dynamics and in particular, integration opportunities. According to the Economic Commission for Latin America and the Caribbean (ECLAC), the average economic growth for the LAC region has declined significantly: 6.7% in 2021 to 3.7% in 2022 to 1.3% in 2023. Such declining economic growth is occurring in a context already marked by high levels of informality and inequality, overstretched institutions and political instability, which in turn primarily affects the poor and vulnerable, including migrants. Within this difficult social and economic context, migrants face obstacles to integrate economically and socially. The most vulnerable are those that are unable to meet their basic needs (rent, food, education and health costs, etc.) because they face challenges accessing income generating opportunities. To address these barriers and based on the results achieved during Phase I of the WeBelong project, Phase II aims to continue supporting sustainable migrant socioeconomic integration through a comprehensive intervention that focuses on Access to Employment; Entrepreneurship Support; and Capacity Strengthening of Local Authorities and Civil Society.</narrative>
  </description>
